[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934597430","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107078#issuecomment-2934597430","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107078","id":2934597430,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u6mc2","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T10:33:44Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T10:33:44Z","body":"The data argument should be an array of one element with the data in that one array\n\nThis should be documented better though","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934597430/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934625669","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107078#issuecomment-2934625669","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107078","id":2934625669,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u6tWF","user":{"login":"Calandiel","id":10187653,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTg3NjUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10187653?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel","html_url":"https://github.com/Calandiel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T10:41:37Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T10:41:37Z","body":"> The data argument should be an array of one element with the data in that one array\n> \n> This should be documented better though\n\nLike this?\n\n```\nvar image_layers = []\n\nvar output_image = Image.create(im_width, im_height * im_depth, false, Image.FORMAT_RGBAF)\n\nimage_layers.push_back(output_image.get_data())\n\noutput_tex = rendering_device.texture_create(format, view, image_layers)\n```\n\nThis leads to a segfault.\n\nSimilarly, doing a packed byte array directly, also leads to a segfault:\n\n```\n\t\tvar output_data = PackedByteArray()\n\t\tfor b in im_width * im_height * im_depth * 4 * 4: # 4 bytes for 4 color channels\n\t\t\toutput_data.push_back(0)\n\t\tvar image_layers = [output_data]\n\t\toutput_tex = rendering_device.texture_create(format, view, image_layers)\n\t\toutput_tex_uniform = make_uniform_from_texture(output_tex, binding)\n```\n\nIn both cases the error is this:\n```\nERROR: FATAL: Index p_index = 1 is out of bounds (size() = 1).\n   at: get (./core/templates/cowdata.h:219)\n```\nfollowed by a backtrace","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934625669/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934650888","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107078#issuecomment-2934650888","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107078","id":2934650888,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u6zgI","user":{"login":"Calandiel","id":10187653,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTg3NjUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10187653?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel","html_url":"https://github.com/Calandiel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calandiel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T10:47:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T10:48:42Z","body":"Sorry for sending two messages in a row. The above is slightly wrong - I edited a wrong MVP (I made multiple versions when trying to isolate the issue from my larger project).\n\nThe segfault happens if both `depth` and `array_layers` are set to some value not equal to 1, like so:\n\n```\nextends Node\n\n# Texture dimensions\nvar width = 2\nvar height = 2\nvar depth = 2\n\nfunc _ready():\n\tvar rd = RenderingServer.get_rendering_device()\n\t\n\t# Format section\n\tvar format = RDTextureFormat.new()\n\tformat.width = width\n\tformat.height = height\n\tformat.depth = depth\n\tformat.array_layers = depth # <- this line is different than in the MVP \n\tif depth == 1:\n\t\tformat.texture_type = RenderingDevice.TEXTURE_TYPE_2D\n\telse:\n\t\tformat.texture_type = RenderingDevice.TEXTURE_TYPE_3D\n\tformat.format = RenderingDevice.DATA_FORMAT_R32G32B32A32_SFLOAT\n\tformat.usage_bits = RenderingDevice.TEXTURE_USAGE_CAN_UPDATE_BIT | RenderingDevice.TEXTURE_USAGE_SAMPLING_BIT | RenderingDevice.TEXTURE_USAGE_STORAGE_BIT | RenderingDevice.TEXTURE_USAGE_CAN_COPY_FROM_BIT\n\n\t# View section\n\tvar view := RDTextureView.new()\n\n\t# Create data\n\tvar output_data = PackedByteArray()\n\tfor b in width * height * depth * 4 * 4: # 4 bytes for 4 color channels\n\t\toutput_data.push_back(0)\n\tvar image_layers = [output_data]\n\n\tprint('attempting to create a texture...')\n\tvar output_texture = rd.texture_create(format, view, image_layers)\n\tprint('the line above this one shouldnt have errored out')\n\tprint('result: ', output_texture)\n```\n\nI think at least this behavior is undesirable ^^'\n\nWhen only depth is set and all data is passed as in the above example, it seems to work fine.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934650888/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934725685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107078#issuecomment-2934725685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107078","id":2934725685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u7Fw1","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T11:09:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T11:09:53Z","body":"I'm not familiar with how these are laid out, but 3D images internally, but you might be able to look at the code for `RenderingServer.texture_3d_create`, implemented here:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e45cc68092906465df3ea9e820a7c77d602addb1/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp#L966\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934725685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2945257196","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107078#issuecomment-2945257196","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107078","id":2945257196,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vjQ7s","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T16:53:17Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T16:53:17Z","body":"Tested with the MRP and the updated code from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107078#issuecomment-2934650888\n\nThe updated code works correctly. \n\nThe [docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_renderingdevice.html#class-renderingdevice-method-texture-create) don't mention that array textures should have one PackedByteArray per slice, while 3D textures should just contain a single packedbyte array. They should be updated to clarify that fact","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2945257196/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2945375892","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107078#issuecomment-2945375892","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107078","id":2945375892,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vjt6U","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T17:25:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T17:25:05Z","body":"Fixed the crash in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107169\n\nThe crash wasn't a result of array_layers and depth being equal. It happened any time array layers was greater than 0 and a non `_ARRAY` texture type was used. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2945375892/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]